{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he put upon him the tunic, and girded him with the sash</b> — This was the order in which Moses acted, but in the command it says (Exodus 29:5), \"And you shall clothe Aaron with the tunic and with the robe of the ephod,\" because He wished to include the sash among all of them in a single command, and it says (ibid. verse 9), \"And you shall gird them with sashes — Aaron and his sons.\" Behold, he clothed him in the tunic together with the sash, and afterward the robe and the ephod, in the order stated there. And here he gave precedence to \"and he girded him with the band of the ephod\" before placing the breastplate upon him, because Moses knew the procedure of dressing: that upon donning any garment he would always immediately gird him with the girdle made for it — with the sash immediately after the tunic, and with the band immediately after the ephod — and it is not proper that the donning of the ephod involve interruptions. But there it says, \"and the ephod and the breastplate, and you shall fasten it to him with the band of the ephod,\" because there he was brief concerning the matter of the breastplate and did not say that he should place it on the ephod, nor that he should place the Urim and the Thummim there, for he had already commanded all of this in the account of the making of the ephod and the breastplate (ibid. 28)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:51:40.005983596Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}